{'post_id': 47, 'day': 35, 'content': "Looking at implementing NovaMind Assistant? Here's what matters most: the tool itself is solid—output quality is genuinely reliable, and it integrates cleanly into clinical workflows. However, I'd be remiss not to mention the support experience. My recent ticket got shuffled between three different teams with minimal coordination. That's concerning when you're evaluating ROI on a healthcare platform—every hour of staff troubleshooting is billable time lost.\n\nThat said, the assistant's core functionality has meaningfully reduced documentation overhead for our practice. The accuracy on clinical summaries justifies the investment. Just ensure you factor support responsiveness into your decision criteria. It shouldn't be an afterthought.", 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'source_group_id': None, 'group_id': 'S2', 'customer_type': 'small', 'custom_name': None, 'persona_name': 'David Okonkwo'}
{'post_id': 46, 'day': 31, 'content': "ISM just released PMI at 48.9, down 0.5 from last month—still in contraction territory. Mixed signals for us in tech/SaaS: companies are clearly pulling back on discretionary spend, but haven't completely shut the door on necessary investments. This cautious environment is going to define Q1 sales conversations.", 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'source_group_id': None, 'group_id': 'S1', 'customer_type': 'small', 'custom_name': None, 'persona_name': None}
{'post_id': 45, 'day': 28, 'content': "With ISM PMI hovering at 48.5, we're seeing businesses pause on growth-oriented tech investments while remaining cautious on major capex commitments. The companies gaining traction right now are those offering quick ROI and operational efficiency—not ambitious feature sets—so we're advising clients to focus conversations on immediate value delivery rather than long-term transformation stories.", 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'source_group_id': None, 'group_id': 'S1', 'customer_type': 'small', 'custom_name': None, 'persona_name': None}
{'post_id': 44, 'day': 28, 'content': 'At 48.5, the PMI is telling us manufacturing and supply chain activity is barely holding steady—which means our customers are delaying non-essential tech investments and scrutinizing every SaaS renewal for immediate ROI. We\'re seeing budget conversations shift from "growth enablement" to "what problem does this actually solve today," so we\'re doubling down on efficiency metrics and cost avoidance rather than feature roadmaps.', 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'source_group_id': None, 'group_id': 'S1', 'customer_type': 'small', 'custom_name': None, 'persona_name': None}
