155 | Spent the last week integrating NovaMind Assistant into our client workflows. Solid foundation—API docs are clean, latency is predictable, and the core output quality holds up under load.

But here's the friction point: their rate limits feel artificially constrained. Hit the ceiling mid-sprint twice this week. Switched to testing an alternative and immediately got 3x the request headroom on the same tier. Both platforms deliver similar quality, but one doesn't force you to architect around arbitrary throttling.

